# Feature page layout

Related: [front-end-structure.mdc](front-end-structure.mdc), [ui-kit-project.mdc](ui-kit-project.mdc).

Use **`FeaturePage`** and **`PageHeader`** from `@webonone/ui-kit` for route-level pages rendered inside a product shell main content area (e.g. WebOnOne `AppShell` `<Outlet />`).

## Required pattern

- Wrap page body in **`FeaturePage`** — do not hand-roll inline `<h1>` title blocks.
- **Width:** full width of the shell main content (`w-full`) — do not add `max-w-*` on feature page wrappers.
- **Title block:** `title` + optional `description` props, or a custom `header={<PageHeader … />}`.
- **Header actions:** pass primary page actions via `actions` (e.g. “Create theme”).
- **Spacing:** rely on `FeaturePage` **`gap-6`** between header and body — do not add extra top margin on the first child.
- **Horizontal padding:** do not add `px-*` on `FeaturePage` — `AppShell` / `PageShell` own shell padding (`px-2 sm:px-6` on mobile/desktop). Page content should align with the app header automatically.

## Typography

| Element | Classes |
|---------|---------|
| Title | `text-2xl font-semibold` (via `PageHeader`) |
| Description | `text-sm text-muted-foreground` |

## Exceptions (do not use FeaturePage)

- Auth / callback routes (`AuthLayout`, login redirect pages)
- Iframe / embed chrome (`EmbedLayout`, Media picker/upload/viewer embeds)
- Auth forms (`AuthLayout` card — intentional narrow login/register UI)
- Showcase demo pages that intentionally preview other layouts

## Reference implementations

| Consumer | Path |
|----------|------|
| Home | `webonone-v2/frontend/src/features/home/pages/HomePage.tsx` |
| Basic Settings | `webonone-v2/frontend/src/features/settings/basic/pages/BasicSettingsPage.tsx` |
| Companies | `webonone-v2/frontend/src/features/settings/basic/pages/CompaniesPage.tsx` |
| System Theme | `webonone-v2/frontend/src/features/settings/system-theme/pages/SystemThemePage.tsx` |
| Email templates | `email/frontend/src/features/templates/pages/TemplatesPage.tsx` |
| Email queue | `email/frontend/src/features/queue/pages/QueuePage.tsx` |
| Showcase demo | `ui-kit/showcase/src/pages/ComponentsPage.tsx` — Layout section |
| Components | `ui-kit/package/src/layouts/FeaturePage.tsx`, `PageHeader.tsx` |

## Verification

From any service frontend workspace (e.g. `webonone-v2/frontend`, `email/frontend`):

```bash
npm run type-check
npm run lint
```

New feature pages under `features/*/pages/` must import `FeaturePage` unless listed in **Exceptions**.
